---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { bench, benchFull } from '../data/site';
const max = Math.max(...bench.map((x) => x[1]));
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Performance" description="Zinc vs QuickJS and Node.js on ten benchmark kernels.">
  <div class="wrap page-head"><span class="eyebrow">Performance</span><h1>About <span class="grad">13× faster</span> than QuickJS.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Geometric mean of 10 kernels, 2× to 80×. Binaries of 70 KiB, 2 ms startup, ~1.3 MiB RSS. Node.js wins fannkuch; it loses the other nine.</p></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="bars">{bench.map(([n, v]) => <div class="bar"><span>{n}</span><div class="t"><i style={`width:${(v / max) * 100}%`}></i></div><em>{v}×</em></div>)}</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:56px">Wall-clock (median of 5 runs, ms)</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Kernel</th><th>Zinc native</th><th>Zinc sim (node)</th><th>Node.js</th><th>QuickJS</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {benchFull.map((r) => <tr><td><code>{r[0]}</code></td>{r.slice(1).map((v) => <td>{v}</td>)}</tr>)}
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>QuickJS is an interpreter with no JIT — the engine PocketJS embeds, so these are also PocketJS's scripting costs. Every kernel prints one line and the harness asserts all four engines print identical output before recording a time.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">setup</span> Apple M1 Pro, macOS 15.7.4, Apple clang 21, Node v24.14.0, QuickJS 2026-06-04. Reproduce with <code>node scripts/bench.mjs</code>. Full methodology and peak RSS: <a href={`${b}docs/reports/perf/`}>PERF report</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="height:80px"></div>
</Base>
